      "writtenOn": "2024-01-03T23:28:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally, the build is already set up to include the chip-specific config header by setting the [`CHIP` value in the `build.mk`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/board/helipilot/build.mk;l\u003d8-10;drc\u003d29c7712541e8f85c53bac4d23147604585a764d8). For `npcx9`, I would expect [this file](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h) to be automatically included.\n\nIt looks like `SET_RTC_MATCH_DELAY` for STM32F4 was changed in https://crrev.com/c/3688190. (Also, I think there\u0027s a typo in [this description](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/config-stm32f4.h;l\u003d77;drc\u003d71b2ef709dcb14260f5fdaa3ab4ced005a29fb46), where it should be \"min time to set RTC match alarm\". If that looks right, can you create a CL to fix?)\n\n[This code](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/system.h;l\u003d693-694;drc\u003dcc2eda2929a248b5f43161641c5b20418800e52f) mentions `HIB_SET_RTC_MATCH_DELAY_USEC`, so it\u0027s possible that is the macro we should be using instead. I\u0027m not sure if I see that defined anywhere though, so we may want to update that comment if that\u0027s changed.\n\nIn the [RTC implementation for NPCX chips](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/system.c;l\u003d233-243;drc\u003d0bcf0fbafc375d4d44c2b7991d998241674936e4) I don\u0027t see any use of the `MATCH_DELAY`, so we may want to add it to avoid trying to set alarms that are too short.",
      "parentUuid": "8c30b956_068d961d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 40
