      "writtenOn": "2024-01-03T23:28:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For `timer.h` and `atomic.h`, it looks like those includes were just missing (something must have indirectly included it on STM32). You can go ahead and pull that into a separate CL that fixes those includes and we can merge that (https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Include_What_You_Use).\n\nThe functions in `clock-f.c` are specific to the STM32*F*412. AFAIK the equivalents were never implemented for dartmonkey (STM32*H*743).\n\nIt looks like there are some [\"system\" functions for handling the RTC](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/system.h;l\u003d682-704;drc\u003dcc2eda2929a248b5f43161641c5b20418800e52f), which have an [implementation for NPCX chips](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/system.c;l\u003d233-243;drc\u003d0bcf0fbafc375d4d44c2b7991d998241674936e4). I\u0027m not sure why the ST functions don\u0027t use the same API. Generally, things in `system.h` should have chip-specific implementations for each chip.",
